prompt:
Create unit `tasks` and implement `abs_diff`: the absolute difference of a and b, for inputs whose absolute value is at most 1_000_000_000_000_000_000. The contract must state that the result is non-negative and equals a - b or b - a.

Required signature (in unit `tasks`):
fn abs_diff(a: i64, b: i64) -> (r: i64)

reference.code:
spec fn moderate(a: i64, b: i64) -> bool { -1000000000000000000 <= a && a <= 1000000000000000000 && -1000000000000000000 <= b && b <= 1000000000000000000 }

spec fn is_abs_diff(a: i64, b: i64, r: i64) -> bool { r >= 0 && (r == a - b || r == b - a) }

#[effects(pure)]
#[uses(moderate, is_abs_diff)]
fn abs_diff(a: i64, b: i64) -> (r: i64)
    requires moderate(a, b),
    ensures is_abs_diff(a, b, r),
{
    if a >= b { a - b } else { b - a }
}
